{"title":"Minkowski Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Minkowski Inequality</b> states that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f33b4fadb0d70e770c03c0d0926c2418487928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"10\" /> are nonzero real numbers, then for any positive numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b159fdba4b71ff0eb9caee9a10fb34ebfcaad8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{ij}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> the following holds:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71daac56ae03992394e45c8f548177049823457e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^{m}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{ij}^r\\right)^{s/r}\\right)^{1/s}\\geq \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^{m}a_{ij}^s\\right)^{r/s}\\right)^{1/r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"381\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p>Notice that if either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is zero, the inequality is equivalent to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=H%C3%B6lder%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Hölder&#39;s Inequality\">Hölder's Inequality</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Equivalence_with_the_standard_form\">Equivalence with the standard form</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Minkowski_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Equivalence with the standard form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5244515956229ce30aadfa3713f9887ca81e44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;s&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/37240beb31ea2d8a191b3da5a88ea517e734c9e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{ij}:=a_{ij}^s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c723507c04757d0a328cef5aceabf454acf2f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p:=\\frac rs&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"33\" />, the symmetrical form given above becomes\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/adddab5aa0b607e4222a3d6af63ef9c27b05fab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^{m}\\biggl(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_{ij}^p\\biggr)^{1/p} \\geq\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\biggl(\\sum_{j=1}^{m}x_{ij}\\biggr)^p\\right)^{1/p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"309\" height=\"62\" />.</center>\n<p>Putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e673b21137260b4d6eac55a0980468e4cada4c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i:=x_{i1},b_i:=x_{i2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />, we get the form in which the Minkowski Inequality is given most often:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f54de6da54fe8ef65efd057f5f6b0daaff6d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\biggl(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_i^p\\biggr)^{1/p}+ \\biggl(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}b_i^p\\biggr)^{1/p} \\geq\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\Bigl(a_i+b_i\\Bigr)^p\\right)^{1/p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"384\" height=\"57\" /></center>\n<p>As the latter can be iterated, there is no loss of generality by putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Minkowski_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=432791#432791\">AIME 1991 Problem 15</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Minkowski_Inequality&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095628\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 78/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 301/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2668/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.383      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.383      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4336:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018095628 and revision id 168869. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}